<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Deliberately NOT a reference to Cranberry.Transport. The harness re-implements the whole
    client half of the SOE wire (RC4, varint, sequencing, fragments, acks, the bundle envelope
    and the leading-zero escape) so that a bug in the server's transport cannot hide behind a
    test that uses the very same code. See docs/72 "What is shared, and the blind spot".

    Cranberry.Zone is referenced for exactly one thing: ZoneOpcodes.Name, the generated lookup
    from the client's own registrations-1148.json. It is data, not behaviour: a wrong entry can
    only mis-label a failure message, never make an assertion pass.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Cranberry.Zone\Cranberry.Zone.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
